  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "There are two items on a restaurant menu. You are in possession of a biased coin. Describe a method to decide between the two items with equal likelihood using the biased coin.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Toss the coin twice. Choose the first item for $HT$ and the second for $TH$. For $HH$ or $TT$, repeat with a fresh pair of tosses.\n\n$HT$ and $TH$ have equal probability, so each item is equally likely.",
      "worked": "Toss the coin in pairs. Choose the first menu item when the pair is $HT$, and the second when it is $TH$. Discard $HH$ and $TT$ and repeat.\n\nLet $p$ be the probability of heads and $q$ the probability of tails. Independent tosses give\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(HT)&=pq\\\\\\Pr(TH)&=qp.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $pq=qp$, the two accepted outcomes are equally likely. Repeating after identical outcomes therefore gives each menu item probability $\\frac12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
